<title>NORWAY: Norway February CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Norway February CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Norway (SSB) issued the following economic indicator.</p>
<p> NORWAY CONSUMER PRICES    FEB 1997   JAN 1997    FEB 1996</p>
<p>Figures (in percent)</p>
<p>  Month-on-month change     +0.3	 +0.8	   0.0</p>
<p>  Year-on-year change	 +3.3	 +3.0	  +0.9</p>
<p>  Index (base 1979)	  268.6	267.8	 260.1</p>
<p>NOTE -- Eight economists polled by Reuters forecast a year-on-year rise in February of 3.15 percent and for inflation to increase by an average 0.15 percent month-on-month.  </p>
<p>SSB attributed the month-on-month rise to increased prices for clothes, shoes and furniture following annual sales in January and to higher prices for cars and nursery school fees.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
